### Description
When JsonSerializerOptions IgnoreNullValues is true then it won't serialize value type fields having default value.
See below test case as an example:

```c#
        [Fact]
        public void Should_Not_Be_An_Empty_Json_When_IgnoreNullValues_Is_True()
        {
            var options = new System.Text.Json.JsonSerializerOptions()
            {
                IgnoreNullValues = true
            };
            var emptyObj = new { };
            var obj = new
            {
                PlayOrder = 0
            };

            var jsonForEmptyObj = System.Text.Json.JsonSerializer.Serialize(emptyObj, options);
            var json = System.Text.Json.JsonSerializer.Serialize(obj, options);

            Assert.NotEqual(jsonForEmptyObj, json);
        }
```

### Configuration
.NET SDK: 5.0.100-preview.6.20318.15
Windows 10 or Linux image mcr.microsoft.com/dotnet/aspnet:5.0-buster-slim show the same behaviour
Architecture: x64, but doesn't seem specific to it

### Regression?
It is a regression in .NET Core 3.1 it was working as expected.
It was also fine in former .NET 5 versions.

### Other information
I would be happy to help adding the test case to the framework tests if guided.
